=== T114 — ADR-0006 eye-prune calibration battery ===
Model: Opus 5   Date: 2026-07-30   Source: src/eyeprune_battery.zig
Rules: area (Chinese) scoring, Black-positive, positional superko
       (pass exempt), terminal on double pass or is_settled.

=== SECTION A — hand-labelled predicate fixtures ===
Each row asserts whether the shipped predicate MUST fire (KNOWN-GOOD:
the eye is genuine and filling it is dominated) or MUST NOT fire
(KNOWN-BAD: the point is not a genuine eye of an unconditionally
alive group, so removing the move could remove a needed move).

  [KNOWN-GOOD] 3x3 alive group, single-point eye            cell  1 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 3x3 same group, open-territory point         cell  7 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 3x3 same board, opponent's view of the eye   cell  1 W  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 3x3 alive group, 2-point eye space (left)    cell  1 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 3x3 alive group, 2-point eye space (right)   cell  2 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 3x3 FALSE EYE (three unconnected stones)     cell  1 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
        ^ naive all-neighbours-own-stones predicate would say: PRUNE (wrong)
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 3x3 PRUNE-ALL: both eyes of an alive group   cell  1 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 3x3 PRUNE-ALL: second eye                    cell  7 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
        ^ is_settled = TRUE (search terminates before move generation); Black legal board moves = 2, both pruned;
          White legal board moves = 0 (both points are suicide).
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 5x5 two-eye alive group, eye A               cell  1 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 5x5 two-eye alive group, eye B               cell  3 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 5x5 same group, open point below             cell 10 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 5x5 same board, White's view of eye A        cell  1 W  expect prune=false got=false PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 5x5 FALSE EYE (cuttable, no Benson chain)    cell  6 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
        ^ naive all-neighbours-own-stones predicate would say: PRUNE (wrong)
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 5x5 ONE-EYE group (not Benson-alive)         cell  1 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
        ^ naive all-neighbours-own-stones predicate would say: PRUNE (wrong)
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 5x5 dead_white (ADR-0006 anchor), eye at 6   cell  6 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-GOOD] 5x5 dead_white, eye at 18                    cell 18 B  expect prune=true  got=true  PASS
  [KNOWN-BAD ] 5x5 dead_white, capture point at 3           cell  3 B  expect prune=false got=false PASS
